```
intro x hx y hy hxy
have hx' : 0 < T - x := sub_pos.mpr hx   -- hx : x ∈ Iio T
have hxy' : T - y ≤ T - x := sub_le_sub_left hxy T
have hanti : volume (T-x) ≤ volume (T-y) := C.antitoneOn (hy') (hx') hxy'
simpa [forwardReducedVolume] using hanti
```
Goal: `forwardReducedVolume C T x ≤ forwardReducedVolume C T y` = `volume (T-x) ≤ volume (T-y)`. `hanti` is exactly that. ✓. But note `C.antitoneOn` is applied with `(mem_Ioi.mpr (sub_pos.mpr hy))` and `(mem_Ioi.mpr hx')` and `hxy'`. Wait, I wrote `C.antitoneOn (Set.mem_Ioi.mpr (sub_pos.mpr hy)) (Set.mem_Ioi.mpr hx') hxy'`. That's a = T-y, b = T-x, giving `volume (T-x) ≤ volume (T-y)`. ✓.

